WEBVTT

00:00:09.370 --> 00:00:12.640
I'm not so fundamentally enthusiastic

00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:16.380
Even I will participate in this

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:20.150
It's been a long time since we went for a drive

00:00:20.150 --> 00:00:22.410
Everyone is excited

00:00:22.980 --> 00:00:25.280
He's coming too

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:28.820
I may have no chance with him right now

00:00:29.690 --> 00:00:32.560
But I'm definitely going

00:00:33.190 --> 00:00:38.600
If you've got a good poker face

00:00:39.370 --> 00:00:41.740
There will be something

00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:45.810
Let's head to the mountains

00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:48.780
We'll just get sunburned at the sea

00:00:49.910 --> 00:00:53.920
Even though it's coat season

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:58.350
He is completely misunderstanding

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:02.590
What's going on?

00:01:02.590 --> 00:01:06.560
Being this happy

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:14.430
I'm laughing so hard I might burst

00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:22.980
I get choked up when I see his back

00:01:22.980 --> 00:01:30.880
In the whirlpool of an endless smile

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:36.420
I guess this is too simple.

00:01:46.600 --> 00:01:48.200
This would be dressing like Rachel.

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:49.770
No, I can't do that.

00:01:49.770 --> 00:01:51.140
Supposedly it's a date!

00:01:51.470 --> 00:01:52.270
Yup.

00:01:52.270 --> 00:01:52.670
Yup.
I see... Herve did, huh?

00:01:52.670 --> 00:01:54.610
I see... Herve did, huh?

00:01:54.940 --> 00:01:56.570
He's kinda cute, huh?

00:01:57.510 --> 00:01:59.750
Wait, are you jealous, Emilio?

00:01:59.750 --> 00:02:01.180
Don't be silly, I only meant...

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:04.120
Will you stop talking about
other people's business?

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:07.820
Good morning.

00:02:08.090 --> 00:02:08.120
Hey...

00:02:08.120 --> 00:02:09.090
Episode #13
Holiday
Hey...

00:02:09.090 --> 00:02:10.390
Episode #13
Holiday
What are you listening to?

00:02:10.390 --> 00:02:12.630
Episode #13
Holiday

00:02:12.630 --> 00:02:13.190
Episode #13
Oh, that song! The one that they play
in the TV commercial all the time!

00:02:13.190 --> 00:02:16.630
Oh, that song! The one that they play
in the TV commercial all the time!

00:02:16.630 --> 00:02:17.770
Oh, yeah?

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:19.290
You don't watch TV much, Claire?

00:02:19.730 --> 00:02:21.240
It's more like, I don't have one.

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:23.830
Oh, yeah, that's right.

00:02:28.340 --> 00:02:30.040
You're in a good mood, huh?

00:02:30.580 --> 00:02:35.350
If someone saw you right now, I don't think
they'd ever suspect the situation we're facing.

00:02:36.950 --> 00:02:38.210
I think it's a good thing.

00:02:39.090 --> 00:02:40.780
They can be too nosey sometimes, you know.

00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:44.250
I don't know why.

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:49.750
Is it because now that I know I might survive,
I've got one less thing to worry about?

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:52.330
Or...

00:02:52.330 --> 00:02:53.960
You have changed, Paula!

00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:56.970
Why would you continue to protect Kate?!

00:02:56.970 --> 00:02:57.970
Jessica...

00:02:57.970 --> 00:03:00.840
Grace exists as a functional unit
because of your presence!

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:07.210
So if everyone stops trusting you,
Paula, Grace will be...

00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:11.610
If it's Kate who changed you, I will...

00:03:14.120 --> 00:03:15.420
I will...

00:03:16.790 --> 00:03:18.350
never forgive her.

00:03:20.930 --> 00:03:22.120
Jessica...

00:03:24.170 --> 00:03:25.670
Go back to your class now.

00:03:25.670 --> 00:03:28.900
If a member of Grace is late for class, it sets a
bad example for the other students, right?

00:03:29.240 --> 00:03:30.710
Paula...

00:03:30.710 --> 00:03:34.270
Besides, I'm not afraid to change.

00:03:39.910 --> 00:03:41.970
All right, class, quiet please!

00:03:42.420 --> 00:03:43.910
I'm going to distribute some handouts...

00:03:44.590 --> 00:03:46.380
Hey, quiet!

00:03:49.390 --> 00:03:52.430
Page 54, translate the third line.

00:03:52.430 --> 00:03:55.260
Page 61, the second paragraph
on the lower right.

00:03:55.260 --> 00:03:57.070
Excuse me, what did you just say?

00:03:57.070 --> 00:03:58.760
I just told you what was going
to be on the next test.

00:03:58.900 --> 00:04:00.400
What? Seriously?!

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:02.370
We'll be quiet, so say it again!

00:04:02.600 --> 00:04:04.540
Should I or should I not?

00:04:04.910 --> 00:04:09.780
Jeez! Look at them, being
manipulated by her again!

00:04:09.780 --> 00:04:13.650
A woman like her who appears to be ditzy
can be pretty devious, you know.

00:04:13.650 --> 00:04:15.050
Don't you think so, Rachel?

00:04:15.420 --> 00:04:17.190
"Devious," huh?

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:18.150
All right, then be quiet, okay?

00:04:18.150 --> 00:04:18.920
What?

00:04:18.920 --> 00:04:19.090
What?
Nothing.

00:04:19.090 --> 00:04:19.290
You're gonna be quiet? Promise, promise?
What?
Nothing.

00:04:19.290 --> 00:04:19.990
You're gonna be quiet? Promise, promise?
Nothing.

00:04:19.990 --> 00:04:20.090
You're gonna be quiet? Promise, promise?

00:04:20.090 --> 00:04:21.020
You're gonna be quiet? Promise, promise?
The study hall is just going to put me to sleep.

00:04:21.020 --> 00:04:21.120
The study hall is just going to put me to sleep.

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:22.090
So if I stay quiet, you're gonna tell us which
part is going to be in the test again?
The study hall is just going to put me to sleep.

00:04:22.090 --> 00:04:24.290
So if I stay quiet, you're gonna tell us which
part is going to be in the test again?

00:04:25.330 --> 00:04:26.060
I don't know!

00:04:26.060 --> 00:04:26.430
Come on!
I don't know!

00:04:26.430 --> 00:04:27.020
Come on!

00:04:35.770 --> 00:04:38.310
They're messages left on a message
board on the internet.

00:04:38.310 --> 00:04:41.980
They're talking about the possible connections
between those girls' suicide cases.

00:04:41.980 --> 00:04:44.470
It's nothing but ridiculous, made-up theories.

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:46.870
Actually, this one is pretty good.

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:49.510
But the thing is, the reality is
more like a fabrication.

00:04:50.020 --> 00:04:51.020
Then...

00:04:51.020 --> 00:04:53.690
Looks like we jumped the gun a little.

00:04:53.690 --> 00:04:56.420
In fact, that detective is becoming quite
persistent in investigating this.

00:04:56.420 --> 00:04:59.760
Adding more members will be
difficult for a while.

00:05:00.560 --> 00:05:03.050
We just have to try to maintain
the current members.

00:05:04.100 --> 00:05:07.830
And in order to do that, your
assistance is necessary.

00:05:08.800 --> 00:05:12.970
You must keep your eyes on the enemies
who try to get close to those girls.

00:05:13.270 --> 00:05:15.670
Yes, we're looking into that right now.

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:19.180
Hello.

00:05:20.680 --> 00:05:23.790
I understand that you guys are in the
middle of an important discussion,

00:05:23.790 --> 00:05:25.510
but would you like to take a quick break?

00:05:25.850 --> 00:05:29.550
This tea is very rare, the first flush of this year.

00:05:29.760 --> 00:05:31.490
We appreciate it.

00:05:34.160 --> 00:05:36.630
Relax and enjoy the aroma of this excellent tea.

00:05:36.630 --> 00:05:41.400
A relaxed mind may come up with great
ideas. Isn't that right, President?

00:05:41.400 --> 00:05:42.430
Sure...

00:05:47.810 --> 00:05:49.040
Rachel...

00:05:49.810 --> 00:05:51.080
Amanda...

00:05:51.080 --> 00:05:52.440
What was that about earlier?

00:05:53.980 --> 00:05:55.420
What are you talking about?

00:05:55.420 --> 00:05:56.910
I didn't do anything.

00:05:57.850 --> 00:05:58.650
What?!

00:05:58.650 --> 00:05:58.950
I want you to come with me.
What?!

00:05:58.950 --> 00:05:59.890
I want you to come with me.

00:06:01.160 --> 00:06:03.190
Hey, you're hurting me!

00:06:03.190 --> 00:06:04.350
Stay right here.

00:06:05.190 --> 00:06:06.330
What's going on?

00:06:06.330 --> 00:06:07.520
I'm...

00:06:12.030 --> 00:06:13.190
Luke...

00:06:13.900 --> 00:06:15.230
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:06:16.100 --> 00:06:17.370
Where should we go?

00:06:17.370 --> 00:06:19.570
Before that, there's something
I need to talk to you about.

00:06:20.140 --> 00:06:21.200
What?

00:06:23.540 --> 00:06:26.510
I am serious about you.

00:06:26.750 --> 00:06:27.850
What?

00:06:27.850 --> 00:06:29.320
I would never give you problems!

00:06:29.320 --> 00:06:33.880
If you called for me, I'd come running for you,
even in the middle of the night!

00:06:34.320 --> 00:06:37.760
And if we went to a party together, I'd be
standing right next to you with a smile! Always!

00:06:38.130 --> 00:06:41.360
And I'll never leave you alone, Luke.

00:06:41.360 --> 00:06:43.260
But, Amanda, I...

00:06:43.260 --> 00:06:44.600
Don't say it just yet!

00:06:45.570 --> 00:06:50.700
Try to take some time and look at me!

00:06:51.340 --> 00:06:51.910
Amanda...

00:06:51.910 --> 00:06:52.470
I won't be like Ra...
Amanda...

00:06:52.470 --> 00:06:53.410
I won't be like Ra...

00:06:54.980 --> 00:06:57.970
I don't mind waiting,
no matter how long it takes.

00:06:58.380 --> 00:07:03.380
I'll be waiting until you
understand how I feel, Luke!

00:07:03.380 --> 00:07:03.890
Amanda...

00:07:03.890 --> 00:07:04.520
I don't need to hear your answer right now!
Amanda...

00:07:04.520 --> 00:07:05.580
I don't need to hear your answer right now!

00:07:06.820 --> 00:07:11.420
It's just that, I wanted you to know
how I feel about you.

00:07:13.230 --> 00:07:14.350
So...

00:07:20.670 --> 00:07:22.970
We couldn't find any leads today after all.

00:07:22.970 --> 00:07:25.910
I know. I'm sorry that I dragged
you with me all day.

00:07:25.910 --> 00:07:26.870
It's okay.

00:07:28.240 --> 00:07:30.310
You're worried about your father, huh?

00:07:30.310 --> 00:07:35.940
If this was a book or a movie, I'd find out he's
got a girlfriend or something, right?

00:07:36.020 --> 00:07:37.020
What?

00:07:37.020 --> 00:07:37.550
Sara?

00:07:37.550 --> 00:07:40.760
Oh, stop it! It's so not like you
to say stuff like that!

00:07:40.760 --> 00:07:44.750
You think so? I know a thing or two about men...

00:07:46.030 --> 00:07:47.930
I mean, I know people who know
a thing or two about men.

00:07:48.230 --> 00:07:52.220
Rose, try not to think about
weird stuff like that, okay.

00:07:56.900 --> 00:07:58.770
Damn, this isn't good.

00:07:58.770 --> 00:08:00.640
There are two of them.

00:08:12.720 --> 00:08:13.810
Kate!

00:08:15.190 --> 00:08:17.680
Stay back! I said stay back!

00:08:18.960 --> 00:08:20.830
No! Stop it! No!

00:08:24.730 --> 00:08:26.100
Hurry, Rose!

00:08:28.700 --> 00:08:29.860
Rose!

00:08:31.240 --> 00:08:32.730
What are you doing?!

00:08:53.690 --> 00:08:55.160
Kate...

00:08:55.160 --> 00:08:56.690
This power...

00:09:20.320 --> 00:09:21.620
Holy shit...

00:09:21.790 --> 00:09:24.290
Claire, how am I supposed to get down?

00:09:24.290 --> 00:09:25.880
You just flew up there, didn't you?

00:09:28.400 --> 00:09:29.950
The hell with you!

00:09:51.750 --> 00:09:53.150
Are you okay?

00:09:59.060 --> 00:10:00.900
Thank goodness, everyone's safe.

00:10:00.900 --> 00:10:02.230
Don't give me that crap!

00:10:02.230 --> 00:10:04.560
I'm sorry! I'm really sorry, Rachel!

00:10:05.630 --> 00:10:10.000
I know it was my fault. Oh my god, you're
bleeding so much. I know it hurts.

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:11.870
Hey, just come to my house so I
can treat the wound...

00:10:11.870 --> 00:10:13.010
What's your deal?

00:10:13.010 --> 00:10:14.140
What?

00:10:14.140 --> 00:10:16.810
All you do is whine like a baby
and you're totally useless!

00:10:16.810 --> 00:10:18.210
Come on, Rachel.

00:10:18.210 --> 00:10:21.080
Seriously, I'm sorry. But I promise
I'll do better next time!

00:10:21.080 --> 00:10:25.250
Stop it! You say that, but you'll just drag
everyone down again, won't you?!

00:10:25.250 --> 00:10:26.880
If that's how it's gonna be,
just don't do anything at least!

00:10:27.250 --> 00:10:28.660
Go hide somewhere and do not come out!

00:10:28.660 --> 00:10:29.690
But I...

00:10:29.690 --> 00:10:31.420
If you don't, I'm the one who's
going to be in danger!

00:10:31.930 --> 00:10:35.660
So please! I'm begging you!
Stop getting in our way!

00:10:44.270 --> 00:10:45.330
Rose!

00:10:47.140 --> 00:10:49.870
I'm not gonna do this with her anymore!

00:10:50.380 --> 00:10:52.080
I think you guys should baby-sit
her starting next time!

00:10:52.080 --> 00:10:53.110
You didn't have go that far!

00:10:53.110 --> 00:10:55.320
What are you talking about? I almost died!

00:10:55.320 --> 00:10:56.220
I know, but...

00:10:56.220 --> 00:11:00.090
This may be a problem.
I don't wanna die either, you know.

00:11:00.090 --> 00:11:01.320
How could you say it like that?

00:11:01.320 --> 00:11:02.690
Then let me ask you this.

00:11:02.690 --> 00:11:05.860
Would you be okay if you died because
the person right in front of you

00:11:05.860 --> 00:11:08.290
wouldn't do anything but cry?!

00:11:27.880 --> 00:11:29.180
Kate?

00:11:30.520 --> 00:11:33.280
Lise, there's no one here by that name.

00:11:33.850 --> 00:11:35.220
Where is Kate?

00:11:35.790 --> 00:11:38.820
I have something I need to give to her.

00:11:39.160 --> 00:11:40.290
Give to her?

00:11:40.290 --> 00:11:41.460
Call Dr. Bender.

00:11:41.460 --> 00:11:42.460
Have the medication ready.

00:11:42.460 --> 00:11:43.590
Yes.

00:11:53.070 --> 00:11:54.470
That moment...

00:12:35.850 --> 00:12:37.150
Kate?

00:12:41.390 --> 00:12:43.290
You're awesome, Kate.

00:12:43.520 --> 00:12:44.830
It's not like that.

00:12:44.830 --> 00:12:47.890
On the other hand, I'm so useless.

00:12:48.900 --> 00:12:51.360
No, not only that...

00:12:52.430 --> 00:12:53.560
Rose...

00:12:54.340 --> 00:12:56.060
Kate, show me how!

00:12:56.470 --> 00:13:00.070
Stuff like what you did earlier!
I don't think I can do it right off the bat,

00:13:00.470 --> 00:13:02.470
but I still want you to show me how to fight!

00:13:02.780 --> 00:13:04.880
But...

00:13:04.880 --> 00:13:08.580
I wanna do what I can too!
I don't wanna be a burden to everyone.

00:13:09.480 --> 00:13:11.420
I don't wanna run away anymore.

00:13:18.490 --> 00:13:19.790
Lise...

00:13:21.930 --> 00:13:24.990
Hey, take a look at this.
Does it remind you of something?

00:13:31.970 --> 00:13:34.200
I'm going to see Kate, you know.

00:13:35.240 --> 00:13:36.710
Are you jealous?

00:13:46.650 --> 00:13:47.950
You did well.

00:13:48.990 --> 00:13:52.930
I can sleep all day because I'm off today.
How about you, Kate?

00:13:55.260 --> 00:13:56.830
I have a date after this.

00:13:56.830 --> 00:13:59.100
What? With the guy you were
talking about before?

00:13:59.100 --> 00:13:59.670
Yeah...

00:13:59.670 --> 00:14:00.130
Oh, no, I'm so sorry!
Yeah...

00:14:00.130 --> 00:14:01.370
Oh, no, I'm so sorry!

00:14:01.370 --> 00:14:03.000
I wouldn't have asked you to help me
practice if I knew about this!

00:14:03.000 --> 00:14:08.340
It's okay, I was nervous about it,
so I feel better now that I exercised.

00:14:17.820 --> 00:14:19.120
I'm sorry!

00:14:19.590 --> 00:14:20.990
It looks good on you.

00:14:20.990 --> 00:14:21.960
What?

00:14:22.920 --> 00:14:28.400
Well, I thought it'd look like an outfit for young
people if it was a bit shorter, but...

00:14:28.400 --> 00:14:29.560
"Young people"?

00:14:42.740 --> 00:14:45.470
It doesn't even leave a scar, huh?

00:14:57.830 --> 00:14:59.120
Rachel...

00:14:59.760 --> 00:15:01.500
I didn't know you were here.

00:15:01.500 --> 00:15:02.560
What a coincidence, huh?

00:15:02.560 --> 00:15:04.060
Yeah, it is.

00:15:04.060 --> 00:15:04.900
Welcome.

00:15:04.900 --> 00:15:06.200
Can I get the same thing he's having?

00:15:06.730 --> 00:15:07.740
Huh?

00:15:07.740 --> 00:15:08.860
Nothing.

00:15:11.810 --> 00:15:13.430
Bitter!

00:15:15.210 --> 00:15:17.800
This shop's espresso is extremely bitter.

00:15:18.580 --> 00:15:20.450
I can't believe you can actually drink this stuff.

00:15:20.450 --> 00:15:25.790
I let it numb my brain so I can forget about
all the negative things and my worldly cares.

00:15:25.790 --> 00:15:26.390
What?

00:15:26.390 --> 00:15:27.390
People used to treat coffee just
like alcohol back in the day.
What?

00:15:27.390 --> 00:15:29.860
People used to treat coffee just
like alcohol back in the day.

00:15:30.320 --> 00:15:31.760
So. I'll take this away from you.

00:15:32.590 --> 00:15:33.290
How about cafe au lait?

00:15:33.290 --> 00:15:34.030
It's okay, I'll drink it!
How about cafe au lait?

00:15:34.030 --> 00:15:35.300
It's okay, I'll drink it!

00:15:35.300 --> 00:15:37.300
Especially, if I can forget about
negative things with it...

00:15:37.300 --> 00:15:38.570
You shouldn't forget about them.

00:15:38.570 --> 00:15:39.670
What?

00:15:39.670 --> 00:15:41.500
Humans are tougher than you think.

00:15:41.500 --> 00:15:44.470
Time can heal even emotional scars on its own.

00:15:45.040 --> 00:15:47.410
Scars can be healed on their own?

00:15:48.410 --> 00:15:52.070
It's going to be healed eventually, so I think you
should face it to the fullest for now.

00:15:52.480 --> 00:15:55.280
You won't even have the strength to do
that once you get old anyway.

00:16:32.120 --> 00:16:34.860
Wow, look how many you've got.

00:16:34.860 --> 00:16:36.320
They said you're supposed to feed them this.

00:16:36.820 --> 00:16:37.830
Chicken?

00:16:37.830 --> 00:16:40.120
Don't you think their food costs more
than they do themselves?

00:16:40.930 --> 00:16:42.090
You've got a point.

00:16:48.740 --> 00:16:50.830
Can I say one thing?

00:16:51.410 --> 00:16:53.010
About those two?

00:16:53.010 --> 00:16:54.700
No, it's a more fundamental issue.

00:16:54.980 --> 00:16:56.600
Then don't say anything.

00:16:59.310 --> 00:17:02.810
It feels like I've done lots of
"first-time-ever" things today.

00:17:03.320 --> 00:17:04.550
Going to Coney Island?

00:17:04.550 --> 00:17:08.490
No, I actually came here a long time ago.

00:17:08.960 --> 00:17:10.120
So, what is it then?

00:17:10.420 --> 00:17:15.120
Umm, it's like a feeling that
I've never felt before.

00:17:22.270 --> 00:17:23.270
Come with me.

00:17:23.270 --> 00:17:24.300
Huh?

00:17:24.300 --> 00:17:26.800
I'll treat you to the best dinner ever.

00:17:36.950 --> 00:17:38.690
It's good.

00:17:38.690 --> 00:17:40.690
Are you sure you didn't mean to say "too spicy"?

00:17:40.690 --> 00:17:44.930
Just a little. It's spicy, but it still tastes good.

00:17:44.930 --> 00:17:46.420
Is this just like you expected?

00:17:47.590 --> 00:17:50.760
Actually, I was expecting
something a little different.

00:17:50.760 --> 00:17:53.330
Really? But this is supposedly your favorite...

00:17:53.330 --> 00:17:55.270
I'm not talking about the chili dog right now!

00:17:56.200 --> 00:17:57.910
You look like a kid when you smile.

00:17:57.910 --> 00:18:03.480
No way! Ever since I was younger,
everyone's told me I'm such a square.

00:18:03.480 --> 00:18:05.210
But you don't look that way.

00:18:06.910 --> 00:18:09.780
Maybe it's thanks to my friends.

00:18:10.150 --> 00:18:11.290
Your friends?

00:18:11.290 --> 00:18:15.420
Yeah, they've always been my classmates,
but I never even spoke to them before,

00:18:15.960 --> 00:18:17.930
but we kind of became friends recently.

00:18:17.930 --> 00:18:22.700
Everyone is completely different. Oh, actually,
four of us are always hanging out together.

00:18:22.700 --> 00:18:25.500
I see, four of you hanging out together, huh?
What do you guys do?

00:18:25.500 --> 00:18:30.460
What do we do? Well, we do exercise and stuff.

00:18:30.970 --> 00:18:31.840
Play sports?

00:18:31.840 --> 00:18:32.070
Uh...
Play sports?

00:18:32.070 --> 00:18:33.040
Uh...

00:18:34.680 --> 00:18:35.700
Excuse me.

00:18:37.640 --> 00:18:39.170
Yes, hello?

00:18:39.710 --> 00:18:41.510
Hmm? What's wrong?

00:18:45.290 --> 00:18:47.410
Okay, I'll be right there!

00:18:47.890 --> 00:18:51.120
Yeah, just wait for me. See you later.

00:18:51.760 --> 00:18:53.060
What's wrong?

00:18:53.830 --> 00:18:56.690
I'm sorry! I just remembered that I needed
to take care of something.

00:18:57.160 --> 00:19:00.260
Oh, yeah, I was supposed to go to
my friend's birthday party.

00:19:00.970 --> 00:19:02.560
That's a problem. Where is the party?

00:19:02.970 --> 00:19:03.990
Err...

00:19:05.570 --> 00:19:08.700
At a Japanese restaurant called
Nori Next Door.

00:19:09.040 --> 00:19:10.110
Okay.

00:19:10.110 --> 00:19:14.140
I've heard that they have a great oyster dish.
We should go check it out together next time.

00:19:14.820 --> 00:19:16.250
Yeah, sure.

00:19:16.250 --> 00:19:17.310
I'm sorry.

00:19:40.510 --> 00:19:46.000
I'm sleepy and I feel like I'm floating.
This is a strange feeling.

00:19:47.650 --> 00:19:49.170
Is this...

00:19:57.190 --> 00:19:59.660
Kate... Kate!

00:20:01.660 --> 00:20:02.960
Mom?

00:20:02.960 --> 00:20:05.490
Your school sent me this.

00:20:05.830 --> 00:20:09.170
It says you've been late and absent
from school quite often lately.

00:20:09.670 --> 00:20:15.340
It's all right, you're an adult already.
I'm sure you have a reason, don't you?

00:20:16.380 --> 00:20:18.410
You don't have to tell me if you don't want to.

00:20:18.410 --> 00:20:23.540
But I still have to tell your father about this.
Don't worry, I'll talk to him.

00:20:24.850 --> 00:20:25.850
I'm sorry.

00:20:25.850 --> 00:20:29.690
I'm okay with it, but your father
should know about this.

00:20:31.290 --> 00:20:32.520
I'm sorry.

00:20:39.870 --> 00:20:40.870
Anna!

00:20:40.870 --> 00:20:41.990
Herve!

00:20:48.610 --> 00:20:52.570
How could this happen?
Where's Dr. Bender, Anna?

00:20:55.880 --> 00:20:57.440
Is he with Lise?

00:20:58.620 --> 00:21:00.110
Where are you going, Herve?

00:21:00.450 --> 00:21:02.320
Don't go! Stay here!

00:21:02.660 --> 00:21:03.680
Anna...

00:21:05.490 --> 00:21:06.720
Please...

00:21:07.530 --> 00:21:09.520
You poor thing, Anna...

00:21:10.160 --> 00:21:18.160
Anna, it's all right. I'll protect you.
I won't let anyone harm you.

00:21:28.950 --> 00:21:31.390
My only love sprung from my only hate

00:21:31.390 --> 00:21:33.790
Too early seen unknown, and known too late

00:21:33.790 --> 00:21:38.720
Prodigious birth of love it is to me,
that I must love a loathed enemy

00:21:39.130 --> 00:21:41.560
Step by step, I lost track of time

00:21:41.560 --> 00:21:44.130
And kept on dancing when I met you

00:21:44.130 --> 00:21:46.430
Without knowing the fate that lies in the stars

00:21:46.430 --> 00:21:48.970
I can't stop falling in love

00:21:48.970 --> 00:21:51.540
An unfaithful moon's lacking morals

00:21:51.540 --> 00:21:53.870
Give light to my full-on desire

00:21:53.870 --> 00:21:56.240
Grasping onto fate, I scream out

00:21:56.240 --> 00:21:58.810
"Wherefore art thou Juliet?"

00:21:58.810 --> 00:22:00.610
Go ahead and laugh at it

00:22:01.110 --> 00:22:02.950
And call it stupid love

00:22:03.550 --> 00:22:05.520
Throw it all

00:22:06.020 --> 00:22:07.950
Because I'll be right there

00:22:08.620 --> 00:22:11.060
Oh, my Juliet...

00:22:11.120 --> 00:22:15.500
Tell me God, what do I do

00:22:15.500 --> 00:22:20.730
To make my wishes come true?

00:22:21.100 --> 00:22:25.370
Ah! This is so painful

00:22:25.370 --> 00:22:28.210
I howl into the night sky

00:22:29.640 --> 00:22:36.350
Does everyone go to sleep

00:22:36.350 --> 00:22:39.590
Holding onto a thought like this?

00:22:39.590 --> 00:22:43.890
Ah! Open your eyes right away

00:22:43.890 --> 00:22:46.730
Laugh at it if it's a joke

00:22:46.730 --> 00:22:49.160
Oh, my sweet Juliet

00:22:50.800 --> 00:22:53.270
You who's sleeping and I with no name

00:22:53.270 --> 00:22:54.770
Pelted by tragic rain

00:22:54.770 --> 00:22:56.430
Say good die

00:23:00.610 --> 00:23:03.370
One lie... Wavering feelings...

00:23:04.440 --> 00:23:10.180
After that smile, he reveals his true feelings.

00:23:10.180 --> 00:23:10.750
Episode #1 4
Reason to Fight
After that smile, he reveals his true feelings.

00:23:10.750 --> 00:23:14.520
Episode #1 4
Reason to Fight
